bout district D rows with sname NULL? GROUP BY NULL HAVING AVG>400 yields one NULL row, unless join excludes D (frpm join excludes D as seen). So 6 rows. Thus whether gold uses HAVING AVG or WHERE AvgScrMath >400, result same 6 rows. Great! Evidence \"average of average math\" aligns with HAVING AVG. We can use HAVING AVG(sa.AvgScrMath)>400 to match. If no frpm join? Use above. We'll get 6. Alternatively if gold filters District Name and has no rtype but joins frpm, D excluded anyway. Fine.\n\nq17: rank schools by AvgScrWrite >499, CharterNum not null. Need maybe use frpm.Charter School Number vs schools.CharterNum? Answer column \"CharterNum\" from schools. Chinese says 特许学校编号（CharterNum）. likely schools.CharterNum. Join satscores with schools on cds. Use `WHERE s.CharterNum IS NOT NULL AND sa.AvgScrWrite > 499`. Rank. But if official gold joins frpm? frpm has `Charter School Number` too, no rtype. Question says CharterNum specifically, schools column. Use schools.\n\nq5: Simple count of SAT math avg >400 virtual F. Join satscores with schools. Need handle rtype? D rows may map to schools with Virtual? Let's compute variants."}
